/*
  core/masks/outcome_habituated_clickthrough.spthy -- OPT-IN outcome row: GENERALIZED warning
  habituation (an extension of the outcome matrix, the way interface_hardened_verify extends the
  demand lexicon).

  The default matrix (outcome_policy.spthy) gives Habituated a degraded outcome only for the
  'confirm' class (autoapprove). This row states the STRONGER, cited claim that habituation
  GENERALIZES across similar-looking security dialogs (Anderson, Vance et al., CHI 2015: habituation
  to one warning transfers to novel warnings that look alike): a user habituated by repeated
  confirm dialogs also CLICKS THROUGH the key-verification step without inspecting it --

    Habituated + compare -> credulous   (accepts ANY offered artifact -> a Mistake, like Naive)

  It is opt-in, not global, because profiles P2/P3 prove `mistake_requires_abstraction` under the
  DEFAULT calibration (a compare mistake needs sigma6); a profile that includes THIS row models the
  generalized-habituation hypothesis instead (see secure_email S2: the Proton Trust-key double modal
  habituates, then the click-through accepts a substituted key). Persistent + read-only, seeded
  unconditionally -> closed theory, no sources loop; OnceHabClickthrough bounds the seed.
*/

rule Seed_habituated_clickthrough [color=#9b51e0]:
    [ ]
  --[ SeedHabClickthrough() ]->
    [ !OutcomePolicy('Habituated', 'compare', 'credulous') ]

restriction OnceHabClickthrough:
  "All #i #j. SeedHabClickthrough()@i & SeedHabClickthrough()@j ==> #i = #j"
